This is a fork of DEGAS 2 with some installation and running scripts (which as of now are incomplete). 

This version ships with its own version of FWEB and does the precompiling from that version. Before attempting to compile DEGAS2, one must first compile FWEB with:
```
cd fweb/Web
./configure
make
```
and check that the binaries ftangle and fweave exist there.

All relevant documentation on compiling and running DEGAS 2 is now
contained in the manual. See the section there entitled "Compiling DEGAS 2".
The manual can be found at:

1. In text form as a TeX file in Doc/degas2_all.tex,
2. This directory also contains HTML, PostScript, and PDF versions
   of this same file.
3. These are all accessible via the Web from the URL:

   http://w3.pppl.gov/degas2

DEGAS 2  usage is now governed by a licensing procedure.  Interested
users should complete and submit the form:

https://theory.pppl.gov/research/TheoryCodeLicenseReleaseForm.pdf

DEGAS 2 is maintained with the Git version control system.  Once
a user is granted access, the code can be cloned from:
https://github.com/PrincetonUniversity/degas2

The version of this distribution can be uniquely identified
by a 40 character hexadecimal "hash":  $Format:%H$.
One or more human readable references or tags may also
be used to label this version:  $Format:%d$.


